<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cantonal Rebellion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1873">1873</a>–<a href="/years/1874">1874</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Cantonal Revolution</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cantonal Rebellion was an uprising of intransigent federal republicans in southern and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> during the First Spanish Republic. From July 1873 cities such as Cartagena, Cádiz, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> proclaimed themselves sovereign cantons. Government troops under Pavía and Martínez Campos put down most of them within weeks, though Cartagena held out until January 1874, weakening the republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cantonal-rebellion.jpg" alt="Cantonal Rebellion" width="320" height="281" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Conflictos en la I República Española.svg: Tyk Derivative work: Durero · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rebeli%C3%B3n_cantonal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
